# Shared Constants

Put reusable values in a constants module instead of scattering magic strings/numbers.

## Where constants live

| App | Folder |
|-----|--------|
| Frontend | `apps/intersfrontend/src/constants/` |
| Backend | `apps/intersbackend/src/constants/` |

- Export named constants from small files (e.g. `api.js`, `messages.js`, `status.js`).
- Re-export from `index.js` when it helps imports stay short.
- This monorepo does **not** share one constants package across FE and BE yet. Keep app-specific values in that app. Only introduce a shared package if a mentor asks.

## Naming

- Use `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for true constants: `API_BASE_URL`, `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE`, `HEALTH_PATH`
- Group related values in one object when useful: `export const HTTP_STATUS = { OK: 200, NOT_FOUND: 404 }`

## What belongs in constants

- API path segments used in more than one place (`/health`, `/users`)
- Default limits, timeouts, page sizes
- User-facing status/error message strings reused in UI
- Enum-like sets of allowed values (`ROLES`, `ORDER_STATUS`)

## What does not belong

- Secrets or API keys (use `.env` / `process.env` / `import.meta.env`)
- One-off strings used in a single line of one file
- React components or business logic (those are not constants)

## Usage

```javascript
// apps/intersfrontend/src/constants/api.js
export const HEALTH_PATH = '/health';

// apps/intersbackend/src/constants/paths.js
export const HEALTH_PATH = '/health';
```

Import from the constants folder; do not redefine the same literal in multiple files.
